#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# mellin_convolve

#% text
# `mellin_convolve(f, g, x, y)` gives the Mellin convolution of `f` and `g`: the integral of `f(x) g(y/x)/x` for `x` from 0 to `inf`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `y` is taken positive; a numeric `y` gives a numerical integral.

#% item
# Factors that do not depend on `x` come out of the convolution.

#% item
# `mellin_convolve(f, g, [x1, ...], [y1, ...])` convolves in several variables.

#% item
# When the integral cannot be done the call stays unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
mellin_convolve(exp(-x), 1/(x + 1), x, 0.3)
#% output
#= 1.2225356050805647

#% cell
mellin_convolve(unit_box(x - 1), x, x, y)
#% output
#= (4/3)*y

#% cell
mellin_convolve(3*f(x), g(x), x, y)
#% output
#= 3*mellin_convolve(f(x), g(x), x, y)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `unilateral_convolve`, `mellin_transform`, `integrate`
